M4 validation patch (TASK-02). Call site: dash src/jobs.c:1002 vforkexec, `pid = vfork()` (+ shellexec/tryexec
in the child). M3 class: direct. For a non-interactive shell without job control the vfork child only execs,
so the parent starts the command with posix_spawn, keeping dash's PATH walk and the ENOEXEC -> /bin/sh
fallback. Any spawn failure falls back to the original vfork path (same diagnostics, 126/127). Interactive and
job-control shells keep vfork (tcsetpgrp in the child has no posix_spawn equivalent).
